    "evidence_text": "This paper reviews stateof-the-art approaches and systems for word segmentation in Vietnamese.\n\nHowever, there is a lack of survey of word segmentation studies on Asian languages and Vietnamese as well.\n\nBased on annotated corpora and token-based features, studies used machine learning approaches to build word segmentation systems with accuracy about 94%-97%.\n\nSection V mainly addresses two existing toolkits, vnTokenizer and JVnSegmenter, for Vietnamese word segmentation.\n\nBUILDING MODEL METHODS\tThere are several studies for Vietnamese Word Segmentation during last decade.\n\nFor instance, Dinh et al. started the word segmentation task for Vietnamese with Neural Network and Weighted Finite State Transducer (WFST)  .\n\nMaximum Matching\tMaximum matching (MM) is one of the most popular fundamental and structural segmentation algorithms for word segmentation  .\n\nThis method is a greedy algorithm, which simply chooses longest words based on the dictionary.\n\nMany researchers applied Hidden Markov model to solve Vietnamese word segmentation such as in  ,  and so on.\n\nJVnSegmenter\tJVnSegmenter is a Java-based Vietnamese Word Segmentation Tool developed by Nguyen and Phan.\n\nEVALUATION AND RESULTS\tThis research gathers the results of Vietnamese word segmentation of several methods into one table as show in Table II.",
